          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In general, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology"} homology
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            is not trivial but is concentrated in degree 0 on the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            object. For some applications, though, it is convenient to divide out that contribution such as to have the homology of the point be entirely trivial. This is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em reduced homology
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#reduced_singular_homology Reduced singular homology
          %p
            We discuss the reduced version of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet(X)
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+chain+complex"} singular chain complex
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong augmentation map
              is the homomorphism of abelian groups
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon \colon C_0(X) \to \mathbb{Z}
            %p which adds up all the coefficients of all 0-chains:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↦
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon \colon \colon \sum_{i} n_i \sigma_i \mapsto \sum_i n_i
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since the boundary of a 1-chain is in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of this map, it constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+map"} chain map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon \colon C_\bullet(X) \to \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is regarded as a chain complex concentrated in degree 0.
          #ReducedSingularChainComplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong reduced singular chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde C_\bullet(X)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of the augmentation map, the chain complex sitting in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to \tilde C_\bullet(X) \to C_\bullet(X) \stackrel{\epsilon}{\to} \mathbb{Z} \to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %strong reduced singular homology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_\bullet(X)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              of the reduced singular chain complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde H_\bullet(X) \coloneqq H_\bullet(\tilde C_\bullet(X))
                    \\,.
          %p Equivalently:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong reduced singular homology
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_\bullet(X)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/augmentation"} augmented
              chain complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to C_2(X) \stackrel{\partial_2}{\to} C_1(X) \stackrel{\partial_1}{\to} C_0(X) \stackrel{\epsilon}{\to}
                    \\mathbb{Z} \to 0
                    \\,.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToOrdinaryHomology Relation to ordinary homology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\bullet(X)
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_\bullet(X)
            its reduced singular homology, def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedSingularChainComplex"}
          #RelationBetweenReducedSingularAndSingular.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              there is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mover
                                  %mi H
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≥
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mover
                                  %mi H
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⊕
                              %mi ℤ
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\tilde H_n(X) &amp; for \; n \geq 1
                    \\\
                    \\tilde H_0(X) \oplus \mathbb{Z} &amp; for\; n = 0
                    }
                    \\right.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homology+long+exact+sequence"} homology long exact sequence
              of the defining short exact sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde C_\bullet(C) \to C_\bullet(X) \stackrel{\epsilon}{\to} \mathbb{Z}
              is, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              here is concentrated in degree 0, of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi ϵ
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \to \tilde H_n(X) \to H_n(X) \to 0 \to \cdots \to
                    0 \to
                    \\cdots \to \tilde H_1(X) \to H_1(X) \to 0 \to
                    \\tilde H_0(X) \to H_0(X) \stackrel{\epsilon}{\to}  \mathbb{Z} \to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exactness
              says that all the morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde H_n(X) \to H_n(X)
              for positive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+object"} projective object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to \tilde H_0(X) \to H_0(X) \to \mathbb{Z} \to 0
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+exact+sequence"} split
              (as discussed there) and hence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0(X) \simeq \tilde H_0(X) \oplus \mathbb{Z}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = *
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_0(\epsilon) \colon H_0(X) \to \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde H_\bullet(*) \simeq 0
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a{:href => "singular%20homology#RelationToHomotopyGroups"} Singular homology – Relation to homotopy groups
              we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ℤ
                            %mtd
                              %mi for
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi n
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(*) \simeq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbb{Z} &amp; for \; n = 0
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, it is clear that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \colon C_0(*) \to \mathbb{Z}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
              map.
          %h3#RelationToRelativeHomology Relation to relative homology
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedSingularChainComplex"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
              relative to any base point
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \colon * \to X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde H_\bullet(X)
                    \\simeq
                    H_\bullet(X,*)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Consider the sequence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+subspace"} topological subspace
              inclusions
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi x
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\emptyset \hookrightarrow * \stackrel{x}{\hookrightarrow} X
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a{:href => "relative%20homology#LongExactSequences"} Relative homology - long exact sequences
              this induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence"} long exact sequence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    H_{n+1}(*) \to H_{n+1}(X) \to H_{n+1}(X,*)
                    \\to
                    H_n(*) \to H_n(X) \to H_n(X,*)
                    \\to
                    \\cdots
                    \\to
                    H_1(X) \to H_1(X,*) \to  H_0(*) \stackrel{H_0(x)}{\to}  H_0(X) \to H_0(X,*)
                    \\to 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here in positive degrees we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_n(*) \simeq 0
              and therefore
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exactness
              gives
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H_n(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H_n(X,*)\;\; \forall_{n \geq 1}
            %p
              and hence with prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RelationBetweenReducedSingularAndSingular"}
              isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tilde H_n(X) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} H_n(X,*)\;\; \forall_{n \geq 1}
                    \\,.
            %p
              It remains to deal with the case in degree 0. To that end, observe that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0(x) \colon H_0(*) \to H_0(X)
              is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi id
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi H
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi x
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi H
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mo ≃
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi H
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi ϵ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi H
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ϵ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    H_0(*) &amp;\stackrel{id}{\to}&amp; H_0(*)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{H_0(x)}}\downarrow &amp;{}^{\mathllap{H_0(f)}}\nearrow&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{H_0(\epsilon)}}_\simeq
                    \\\
                    H_0(X) &amp;\stackrel{H_0(\epsilon)}{\to}&amp; \mathbb{Z}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to *
              is the terminal map. That the outer square commutes means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0(\epsilon) \circ H_0(x) = H_0(\epsilon)
              and hence the composite on the left is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_0(x)
              is an injection.
            %p
              Therefore we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
              as shown in the top of this diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi H
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mo ≃
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi H
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi ϵ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    0 &amp;\to&amp; H_0(*) &amp;\stackrel{H_0(x)}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                    H_0(X) &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; H_0(X,*)
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    0
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp; {}_{\mathllap{\simeq}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{H_0(\epsilon)}} &amp;
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; \mathbb{Z}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p Using this we finally compute
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mover
                                %mi H
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mi ker
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ϵ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi coker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\tilde H_0(X)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    ker H_0(\epsilon)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq coker( H_0(x) )
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq H_0(X,*)
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Moreover, for “good” inclusions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow X
              of topological space, the reduced singular homology of the quotient
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X/A
              is isomorphic to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+singular+homology"} relative singular homology
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              See at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "relative+homology#RelationToQuotientTopologicalSpaces"} Relative homology - Relation to reduced homology of quotient topological spaces
          %h3#RelationToWedgeSums Relation to wedge sums
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{* \to X_i\}_i
            be a set of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee_i X_i \in Top
            for their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_i \colon X_i \to \vee_i X_i
            for the canonical inclusion functions.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mover
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\tilde H_n(\iota_i))_i \colon \oplus_i \tilde H_n(X_i) \to \tilde H_n(\vee_i X_i)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            For instance (
            %a{:href => "#Hatcher"}> Hatcher, cor. 2.25
            ).
